.TH GTK4DIALOG 1 "June 2026" "gtk4sermo 1.0.0" "Haplo-Linux User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtk4sermo \- GTK4 dialog box creator for shell scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtk4sermo
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B gtk4sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.br
.B gtk4sermo
\fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
.br
.B gtk4sermo
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
.br
.IR VARIABLE =\(aq<window>...</window>\(aq
.B gtk4sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtk4sermo
reads a GTK4 GUI description written in an XML dialect and displays
the resulting dialog window.
It is designed to be called from shell scripts to present interactive forms,
progress bars, list views, and other widgets without requiring knowledge of
GTK4 programming.
.PP
The GUI description can be supplied from an environment variable
.RB ( \-\-program ),
a file
.RB ( \-\-file ),
or standard input
.RB ( \-\-stdin ).
.PP
When a button action triggers EXIT or REFRESH,
.B gtk4sermo
writes the current value of each named widget to standard output in the form:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
WIDGET_NAME=current_value
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-program= VARIABLE
Read the XML dialog description from the environment variable
.IR VARIABLE .
.TP
.BI \-\-file= FILE
Read the XML dialog description from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read the XML dialog description from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-do= CMD
After the dialog has closed, run the shell command
.IR CMD .
The widget values are exported as environment variables first, so
.I CMD
can read them directly. The command goes through the same path as every other
command the program runs: a direct
.BR exec ()
without a shell when
.I CMD
carries no shell metacharacter, a logged
.B /bin/sh \-c
fallback otherwise, and a clean refusal when
.B HAPLO_NO_SHELL_FALLBACK=1
is set. The exit status of the dialog is not replaced by that of
.IR CMD ;
a non-zero status is reported as a warning.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Widget values are exported as environment variables before executing
.B \-\-do
commands.
.TP
.B HAPLO_NO_SHELL_FALLBACK
When set (to any value), refuse the
.B /bin/sh \-c
fallback used for
.RB < input >/< action >
commands that contain shell metacharacters, and fail closed instead. Commands
without shell metacharacters still run via direct
.BR exec ()
(no shell). Use this to harden gtk4sermo when rendering XML whose command
strings may come from a less-trusted source than the local script author (see
.B safe_exec.c
design note 1).
.TP
.B HAPLO_ALLOWED_CMDS
A comma-separated list of command names that the program is allowed to run, for
example
.BR HAPLO_ALLOWED_CMDS=ls,cat,date .
Unset by default, and deliberately so: the XML language exists to run commands,
and the shipped examples invoke around twenty of them — fourteen call
.B bash
or
.B sh
directly. A list that were on by default would break the product without
protecting anyone, since the command comes from the very script the caller
wrote. It is meant for the other case: someone DEPLOYING a dialog into a
less-trusted context (a kiosk, a guest session) who wants to bound what it can
launch.
.IP
The comparison is on the program's base name, so
.B /bin/ls
and
.B ls
are the same name. While the list is set, the
.B /bin/sh \-c
fallback is refused as well \(em otherwise
.B sh \-c \(aq...\(aq
would walk straight through the list by calling itself
.BR sh .
.TP
.B GTKDIALOG_PIXMAP_PATH
Colon\-separated list of directories in which gtk4sermo searches for image
files that are not found at the path given in the XML. It is consulted when
loading
.BR <pixmap> ,
window and button icons, and menu\-item images.
.TP
.B MAIN_DIALOG
Fallback source variable. When none of
.BR \-\-program ,
.BR \-\-file ,
.BR \-\-stdin ,
.B \-\-event\-driven
or
.B \-\-glade\-xml
is given, gtk4sermo reads the GUI description from the environment variable
named
.BR MAIN_DIALOG .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/gtk4sermo/
Documentation, examples, and reference pages.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/gtk4sermo.1.gz
This manual page.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Simple yes/no dialog
.nf
export DIALOG='
<window title="Confirm">
  <vbox>
    <text><label>Proceed?</label></text>
    <hbox>
      <button ok></button>
      <button cancel></button>
    </hbox>
  </vbox>
</window>'
gtk4sermo --program=DIALOG
.fi
.SS Read entry value
.nf
export DIALOG='
<window>
  <vbox>
    <entry><variable>NAME</variable></entry>
    <button ok></button>
  </vbox>
</window>'
gtk4sermo --program=DIALOG --do='echo "Name: $NAME"'
.fi
